{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/NetworkLib\/documentation\/NetworkLib"]]},"metadata":{"title":"Connecting Through an HTTP Proxy","modules":[{"name":"NetworkLib"}],"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article"},"kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Configure an HTTP CONNECT tunnel with optional authentication."}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/NetworkLib\/documentation\/NetworkLib\/UsingProxies","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"sections":[],"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Related-Documentation","title":"Related Documentation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/NetworkLib\/documentation\/NetworkLib\/SendingAndReceiving"]},{"anchor":"API-usage-examples","title":"API usage examples","identifiers":["doc:\/\/NetworkLib\/documentation\/NetworkLib\/RunningExamples","doc:\/\/NetworkLib\/documentation\/NetworkLib\/SendingAndReceiving","doc:\/\/NetworkLib\/documentation\/NetworkLib\/UsingCallbacks","doc:\/\/NetworkLib\/documentation\/NetworkLib\/TypedMessages","doc:\/\/NetworkLib\/documentation\/NetworkLib\/HTTPHeaders"],"generated":true}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/networklib\/usingproxies"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Use ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/NetworkLib\/documentation\/NetworkLib\/RawSocketConfiguration\/Proxy-swift.struct","type":"reference"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/NetworkLib\/documentation\/NetworkLib\/RawSocketConfiguration\/using(proxy:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" to add a proxy to a destination configuration. Proxy connections require iOS or tvOS 15.4 or later, or macOS 12.3 or later.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Configure a secure proxy connection","anchor":"Configure-a-secure-proxy-connection","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Replace the example proxy hostname and port with those of your proxy. Supply credentials from your application’s credential storage.","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["import NetworkLib","","@available(iOS 15.4, tvOS 15.4, macOS 12.3, *)","func connectThroughProxy(username: String, password: String) async throws {","    let destination = RawSocketConfiguration(","        \"example.com\",","        .https,","        isSecure: true,","        sni: \"example.com\"","    )","    let proxy = RawSocketConfiguration.Proxy(","        host: \"proxy.example.com\",","        port: 8443,","        isSecure: true,","        sni: \"proxy.example.com\",","        authorization: .basic(userName: username, password: password)","    )","    let socket = try RawSocket(destination.using(proxy: proxy))","","    do {","        let info = try await socket.connect()","        print(\"Connected through proxy:\", info.remoteEndpoint)","        \/\/ Exchange destination protocol data here.","        await socket.cancel()","    } catch {","        await socket.cancel()","        throw error","    }","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The proxy in this example must support TLS and HTTP CONNECT. Its ","type":"text"},{"code":"isSecure","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" setting controls TLS to the proxy; the destination configuration controls TLS inside the tunnel. For a plaintext HTTP CONNECT proxy, set the proxy’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"isSecure","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to ","type":"text"},{"code":"false","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and use its appropriate port. Omit ","type":"text"},{"code":"authorization","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" when authentication isn’t required.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"After connecting, send and receive data using the same socket methods as for a direct connection. The library establishes the CONNECT tunnel for you.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Run the CLI example","anchor":"Run-the-CLI-example","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"From a local checkout of NetworkLib, run this command in the directory containing ","type":"text"},{"code":"Package.swift","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":":","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"sh","type":"codeListing","code":["swift run Examples proxy"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Set ","type":"text"},{"code":"NL_PROXY_HOST","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"NL_PROXY_PORT","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for your HTTP CONNECT proxy. For example, with a plaintext proxy listening locally:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"sh","type":"codeListing","code":["NL_PROXY_HOST=localhost NL_PROXY_PORT=8080 NL_PROXY_TLS=false swift run Examples proxy"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"NL_PROXY_TLS","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" defaults to ","type":"text"},{"code":"true","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". For TLS proxies, the certificate must be trusted by the system. If authentication is required, set both ","type":"text"},{"code":"NL_PROXY_USERNAME","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"NL_PROXY_PASSWORD","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in the environment. The CLI fetches ","type":"text"},{"code":"https:\/\/example.com","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" through the proxy and prints the raw response. This command requires macOS 12.3 or later.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The runnable implementation is in ","type":"text"},{"code":"Sources\/Examples\/ProxyExample.swift","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". See ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/NetworkLib\/documentation\/NetworkLib\/RunningExamples","type":"reference"},{"text":" for tool requirements, the complete command list, and shared CLI behavior.","type":"text"}]}]}],"references":{"doc://NetworkLib/documentation/NetworkLib/RunningExamples":{"role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/NetworkLib\/documentation\/NetworkLib\/RunningExamples","type":"topic","kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/networklib\/runningexamples","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Run the documented API examples from the terminal using the repository’s Examples target."}],"title":"Running the Examples"},"doc://NetworkLib/documentation/NetworkLib/HTTPHeaders":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/NetworkLib\/documentation\/NetworkLib\/HTTPHeaders","type":"topic","role":"article","title":"Working with HTTP Headers","abstract":[{"text":"Use typed header keys with Foundation requests.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/networklib\/httpheaders"},"doc://NetworkLib/documentation/NetworkLib/RawSocketConfiguration/Proxy-swift.struct":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/NetworkLib\/documentation\/NetworkLib\/RawSocketConfiguration\/Proxy-swift.struct","kind":"symbol","title":"RawSocketConfiguration.Proxy","role":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/networklib\/rawsocketconfiguration\/proxy-swift.struct","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Proxy"}],"abstract":[{"text":"HTTP CONNECT proxy settings used when creating a proxied socket connection.","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Proxy","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://NetworkLib/documentation/NetworkLib/RawSocketConfiguration/using(proxy:)":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/NetworkLib\/documentation\/NetworkLib\/RawSocketConfiguration\/using(proxy:)","kind":"symbol","title":"using(proxy:)","role":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/networklib\/rawsocketconfiguration\/using(proxy:)","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"using","kind":"identifier"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"proxy"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"RawSocketConfiguration","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:10NetworkLib22RawSocketConfigurationV"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Proxy","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:10NetworkLib22RawSocketConfigurationV5ProxyV"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"RawSocketConfiguration","preciseIdentifier":"s:10NetworkLib22RawSocketConfigurationV"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Returns a copy of this configuration that connects through the specified HTTP CONNECT proxy.","type":"text"}]},"doc://NetworkLib/documentation/NetworkLib/SendingAndReceiving":{"kind":"article","title":"Sending and Receiving Data","abstract":[{"text":"Connect securely, send bytes, and read a response with async\/await.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/NetworkLib\/documentation\/NetworkLib\/SendingAndReceiving","role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/networklib\/sendingandreceiving","type":"topic"},"doc://NetworkLib/documentation/NetworkLib/UsingCallbacks":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/NetworkLib\/documentation\/NetworkLib\/UsingCallbacks","type":"topic","role":"article","title":"Using Completion Handlers","abstract":[{"text":"Connect and send data using the callback-based socket API.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/networklib\/usingcallbacks"},"doc://NetworkLib/documentation/NetworkLib/TypedMessages":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/NetworkLib\/documentation\/NetworkLib\/TypedMessages","type":"topic","role":"article","title":"Exchanging Typed UDP Messages","abstract":[{"text":"Represent a UTF-8 datagram with the socket’s message protocols.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/networklib\/typedmessages"},"doc://NetworkLib/documentation/NetworkLib":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/NetworkLib\/documentation\/NetworkLib","kind":"symbol","title":"NetworkLib","role":"collection","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/networklib","abstract":[{"text":"Build socket connections with Swift concurrency and Apple’s Network framework.","type":"text"}]}}}